      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"Soong installation is only supported for host modules\" is a little misleading, it meant that Soong would install host modules to out/soong/host/linux-x86/bin/, and then Make would install the same module to out/host/linux-x86/bin/, and we wanted the Make location to depend on the Soong location so building the Make location would ensure the Soong location existed and was up to date.\n\nThis CL gets rid of the distinction between \"Make installation\" and \"Soong installation\" by having Soong create the installation rule into the location Make used to use.  There is no longer an out/soong/host/linux-x86/bin/ copy, and keeping line 192 results in a circular dependency.",
